This is a short status report on Pi, not the famous version number of
\TEX\ (among other things), but
the small machine, meant for education but nowadays also used for Internet Of
Things projects, process control and toy projects. While the majority of \TEX\
installations run on an Intel processor, the Raspberry Pi has an \ARM\
central processing
unit. In fact, its main chip has the same foundation as those found in settop
boxes all around the world. It's made for entertainment, not for number
crunching.

